    "final_message": "`scripts/verify story-drafting` passes on the first full run, and the work is committed as `59ae6d7` on the run branch. The gate was clean: zero tessercheck findings, `mypy --strict`, 77 non-root tests, and both acceptance tests against the host on :9350. There is no GAP.\n\n**Domain** (`<repo>/story-drafting/drafting/domain/jtbd.py`)\n- The `Jtbd` contract is unchanged.\n- **Status** is worked out from the stories rather than stored:\n  - no stories: `drafting_stories`\n  - any story still drafted: `awaiting_story_acceptance`\n  - otherwise: `stories_decided`\n- **`record_stories`** gives one of three answers:\n  - `already_recorded` if the job to be done already has stories\n  - `none_given` if it was handed no story texts\n  - `recorded` otherwise, keeping each story text as a drafted story\n- **New value objects:** I added `StoryText` (given/when/then, with a `drafted()` method that returns a drafted `StoryView`) and `StoryTexts`. `StoryTexts` is the only place that reads `RecordStoriesSpec`, which keeps TB083 satisfied. Neither is re-exported, so both are tested through `Jtbd`.\n- `Text` now refuses blank values.\n\n**Drafter** (`.../story-drafting/drafting/adapters/gateways/template_story_drafter.py`)\nIt always returns the same two story texts, filled from role, i_want and so_that:\n- \"I am {role}\" / \"I get {i_want}\" / \"{so_that}\"\n- a variant about stepping away and coming back to the same job to be done\n\n**Tests**\n- `test_jtbd.py` has 11 tests: the spec round-trip, each status, the effect of each outcome, refusing a blank story, and story equality.\n- `test_template_story_drafter.py` has 3.\n\n**Two weak spots in the tests**\n- Each outcome is checked by what it does to the status and stories, not by which outcome comes back. TB084 only allows an outcome member to be named in a `return` or a `case`.\n- The blank-story test uses `pytest.raises(Exception)` rather than the specific tesser error type, so it woul"
  },
